        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I authored <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3694300203\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28575\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28575/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28575\">#28575</a> and put <code class=\"notranslate\">WebAssembly.Memory.prototype.toFixedLengthBuffer()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">WebAssembly.Memory.prototype.toResizableBuffer()</code> in the main <code class=\"notranslate\">webassembly/api.json</code> file. A better location for it is <code class=\"notranslate\">webassembly/api/Memory.json</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">These two methods are supported in Safari 26.2.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Release notes for Safari 26.2: <a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-release-notes/safari-26_2-release-notes\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-release-notes/safari-26_2-release-notes</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Original PR: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3694300203\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28575\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28575/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28575\">#28575</a></p>",
