        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 146 adds support for scroll-driven animations; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5181996801982464\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5181996801982464</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29033\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29033/hovercard\">latest Chrome collector PR</a> has added BCD for several of the related features; my PR adds a few more, namely the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;animation-action&gt;</code> data type, and the related range properties, which <em>are</em> supported but currently under an old name.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29034",
            "title": "Chrome 146 scroll-triggered animations",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-12T15:29:04.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-02-12T15:28:11.000Z",
